      \field{abstract}{We present in this paper Okapi, a web-based application for research communities in social sciences and humanities offering the combined functionalities of Multimedia Content Management Systems and Knowledge Bases. Okapi differentiates from other systems by its extreme genericity, its functional richness and its interoperability with both online institutional archives and the Linked Open Data (LOD). The functionalities of the tool are presented and illustrated by their utilization within different research projects and more especially for the deployment of an institutional portal at the french national institute of oriental languages and civilizations (INALCO).}
