      \field{abstract}{This work is the result of a 6 months internship experience in the ANR Highvision project, dedicated to automatic study of the circulation of press photographs in the early XXth century, and in the PictorIA consortium, an initiative dedicated to the study of AI possibilities for image analysis in Digital Humanities. The said mémoire mainly studies the impact of machine learning technologies in historical research and LAM institutions. It also presents a protocol used for automatic segmentation of newpaper pages based on a custom YOLO model and pero-ocr, and an attempt to tackle the trials of image-text links in the context of press, through the CLIP model.}
